# beside them, an item given another category, the items' commands, the
# Categories dialog adding a category above the one followed, which
# stays selected, and deleting the one followed, a category added,
# renamed, reordered and deleted, a category's items as a screen of
# their own, titled again once the dialog renames it, and ESC back, View
# > Pane beside the list and the splitter's drag; BB, with the
# forty-eight categories of TEST/KEYS/BYCATL.REQ and the sixty items of
# TEST/KEYS/RLLONG.REQ (INVWIN_WINSEEDBB) and the width of
# TEST/WIN/BYCATW.CFG, left as its golden (INVWIN_WINCMPBB), the list
# paged by the client, the counts after an item leaves a category and
# after categories come and go, a category sought over its pages after a
# save and the pane hidden; BC the refusals at level 1 and, at level 2,
# the rename and the refused delete of a category that items have and
# the delete of one that none has, its settings file left as its golden
# (INVWIN_WINCMPBC).  EA to EI choose every row of a list (CTRL-/), on
# the 257 items more of TEST/WIN/mkitems.sh (INVWIN_WINSEEDEA..EG), so
# that a byte does not count them: EA, with the preview
# (INVWIN_WINARGSEA), the count panel, the pages kept selected and every
# key and click that ends it, CTRL-BSLASH in the list and in the preview,
# the Record entry, the pop-up and an Esc stopping the collecting, what
# was chosen kept; EB Move and DEL on all, DEL kept by No and stopped
# after one row by an ESC of the driver's A lines; EC Move, Install in
# and Take out stopped at a refusal in the middle, with item 50 installed
# in item 1 (TEST/KEYS/ALLPART.REQ); ED loans, returns, reservations and
# releases of all; EE level 1, where choosing is allowed and each command
# refused once, the items' audit log unchanged; EF and EH the most rows a
# choice holds, on 4094 and 4117 items more: one row too many refused,
# the rows chosen kept, and, after a delete, 4096 chosen, and a longer
# list's walk stopped early; EG the split view's contents: the tree
# moving under them, a held press and a drag of all; EI, on 300 items
# more, DEL stopped by item 270, which has a part (TEST/KEYS/ALLKID.REQ),
# the list counting the rows left; EJ, with the assemblies of
# TEST/KEYS/PANEA.REQ (INVWIN_WINSEEDEJ) and a settings file that is not
# there (INVWIN_WINARGSEJ), the lists that have a pane and the panes:
# all assemblies chosen with the parts following the focus row, all
# parts taken out, a category's items lent, the loans returned, and the
# categories and a user's audit entries, which take one row.  BK and BL
# go back (ESC) to the row left: BK, with a settings file that is not
# there (INVWIN_WINARGSBK), to the tree from the users, with the focus
# in the tree and in the contents, and from an item's parts opened in
# the contents; BL, on the items of EH
# (INVWIN_WINSEEDBL), to a row beyond the rows a seek passes, so to the
# first, and to one within them.  CV has the frame painted again as
# after a switch to another program and back (the driver's C line), with
# the focus in the item list, the location tree and its contents, and
# the locations' pick list so too: no row is left blank.  PF, with the
# rooms of TEST/mkrooms.sh (INVWIN_WINSEEDPF), as many as a seek passes,
# moves Crate: its pick list opens where the seek for its room gave up,
# OK there asks first and No keeps the dialog, Cancel moves nothing, and
# the top level chosen moves it without a question.  IK has INS and DEL
# with SHIFT or CTRL, the clipboard keys, do nothing on the item list and
# in the Categories dialog, where INS and DEL alone still add and delete.
# Every
# other script runs with TEST/WIN/INV.CFG beside it, whose WINPANE lines
# keep the item lists, the assemblies, the loans and the users alone,
# but J, N, O, RA, RB and RC, whose settings files have no such line,
